<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nekor</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Nakur</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nekor was a town in the Rif of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-hoceima">Al Hoceima</a>, founded in the early 9th century as the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Nekor. It stood in the fertile valley of the Nekor river, a short distance from the sea, and traded with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> raided it in 859. It declined in the 11th century and was destroyed in the Almoravid conquest.</p></div>
